1	/* =====================================================================
2	 * measure_envelope.c — TASK-20260810-2a0a37 (GOAL-AES-002 / BATCH-2b0fd1)
3	 *
4	 * PURPOSE. Toolchain-and-throughput benchmark ONLY. It resolves by
5	 * measurement whether gcc with -maes compiles and runs on this host and
6	 * at what rate this implementation performs AES-128 block operations.
7	 * It performs NO cryptanalysis, attempts no key recovery, computes no
8	 * distinguisher, and asserts NOTHING about AES security at any round
9	 * count. Any infrastructure failure of this program is infrastructure
10	 * signal, never negative mathematical evidence about AES (AGENTS.md
11	 * rule 5). This artifact is infrastructure and is expressly NOT a
12	 * completion (GOAL-AES-002 non_completion_criteria (vi)).
13	 *
14	 * DESIGN NOTES.
15	 *  - The S-box and Rcon table are COMPUTED at startup from the AES
16	 *    definition (GF(2^8) inversion under the modulus polynomial, then
17	 *    the affine map; Rcon by GF doubling). No table is transcribed from
18	 *    memory. Correctness is established at runtime by the driver, which
19	 *    cross-checks this program's outputs on random vectors against TWO
20	 *    independent implementations (pycryptodome and the openssl CLI),
21	 *    which is the specification pinning discipline of RQ-AES-002.
22	 *  - Round transformations use AES-NI intrinsics (_mm_aesenc_si128 /
23	 *    _mm_aesenclast_si128); the key expansion is scalar C.
24	 *  - bench modes:
25	 *      fresh : per iteration, expand a FRESH key and encrypt one block
26	 *              (the CM-1 AEU-128 shape: schedule charged, not amortised).
27	 *      dep   : one expanded key, blocks in a DEPENDENT chain (output feeds
28	 *              input) — latency-bound, no cross-block pipelining.
29	 *      ind   : one expanded key, INDEPENDENT blocks — throughput-bound,
30	 *              pipelining across blocks allowed.
31	 *  - Timing by CLOCK_MONOTONIC. The xor-accumulator prevents the work
32	 *    being optimised away; it is printed with every result line.
33	 *
34	 * ------------------- COMMENT-BLOCK INFERENCE STANZA -------------------
35	 * authored_by_task: TASK-20260810-2a0a37
36	 * authored_by_role: executor
37	 * handoff_inference_policy: executor-implementation
38	 * handoff_reasoning_effort: null (policy default)
39	 * fallback_used: false
40	 * degraded_allowed: false
41	 * degraded_requirements: []
42	 * resolved_model_id: null (not surfaced by this runtime; unverified
43	 *   configuration until a doctor --probe confirms a backend serves it)
44	 * resolved_runtime: claude-code session (api_direct-equivalent tool set)
45	 * bedrock: NOT selected, configured, probed or contacted, and never may
46	 *   be (AGENTS.md rule 16; task constraint SC-11)
47	 * claim_tier_of_this_artifact: infrastructure measurement only; states
48	 *   no margin, no cryptanalytic claim, and nothing about AES at any
49	 *   round count; the R5 anti-laundering clause of RQ-AES-002 applies to
50	 *   any later record that quotes this program's numbers in a margin.
51	 * -----------------------------------------------------------------------
52	 * ===================================================================== */
